    <td>
      <p align="center"><u><b><i><font size="4" color="#FFFFFF">GUILD
      MOTTO:&nbsp;</font></i></b></u><font size="4" color="#8000FF"><u><br>
      </u><br>
      </font><font color="#8000FF" size="3"><b>                   Debeo amicitia; nos an
      unus!&nbsp;</b></font><font size="4" color="#8000FF"><br>
      <br>
      </font><b><font color="#8000FF" size="3">                Bound by friendship; we are one!&nbsp;</font></b><font size="4" color="#8000FF"><br>
      <br>
      </font><b><u><i><font size="4" color="#FFFFFF">GUILD CHARTER:&nbsp;</font></i></u></b></p>
      <p align="left"><font color="#8000FF" size="3"><b>     UNC is a Guild banded together by friendship. The members of the Guild are dedicated to assisting each other      thru the difficult times that can plague our lives in  Norrath. We have united together under one name to do      battle against the villainous minions that roam the    continents and, best of all, we have vowed to have fun                       together while doing it!&nbsp;</b></font></p>
      <p align="left"><font color="#8000FF" size="3"><b>Each and every Guild member should keep in mind that while they are traveling
      through Norrath, they will be viewed as representatives for the Guild. Because of
      this, Guild members should always act in ways that present the Guild and its
      members in a positive light. The Guild will *not* tolerate stealing, lying, or
      disrespectful behavior from its members. Every Guild member is greatly encouraged
      to utilize the tools (i.e.-the message board) the Guild has to offer as well as seek
      out other Guild members for grouping and assistance. Using special trade skills
      or other abilities for fellow Guild members is also strongly encouraged, however,
      it is important to keep in mind that each Guild member has worked hard to get
      where they are now and their skills and services should not be taken for granted.
      Although many Guild members may be very generous with their time, money, or
      extra items, no Guild member should expect to be power-leveled nor should they
      expect that items be given to them that they did not earn themselves.</b></font></p>
      <p align="center"><u><i><b><font size="4" color="#FFFFFF">GUILD HISTORY:</font></b></i></u></p>
      <p align="left"><b><font color="#8000FF" size="3">Soulblaze and Synew, the closest of friends, had traveled
      far and wide thru the land of Norrath looking for a Guild  they could one day consider home. Disillusioned by some,  they resigned themselves to fighting side by side with good                 friends, but apart from any Guild.&nbsp;<br>
      <br>
  Far across the land, the Stormfyre family was growing by    leaps and bounds. They also dreamed of a Guild worthy    enough to join...one that would be their second family.&nbsp;&nbsp;</font></b></p>
      <p align="left"><b><font color="#8000FF" size="3">
   When these two groups of people met and combined their forces on January 24th
      in the year 2000, they became...</font></b></p>
      <p align="center"><b><u><i><font size="4" color="#FFFFFF">                   The United Norrath Coalition&nbsp;</font></i></u></b></p>
      <p align="left"><b><font color="#8000FF" size="3">M</font></b><b><font color="#8000FF" size="3">ost
      recently, Soulblaze and Synew have joined up with our esteemed allies,
      Legion of Fate, leaving the Guild in the hands of Anavrin Stormfyre, who
      with the help of the Guild Officers, Bridgecrusher Dabashar, Etha
      Tanglewood, Faedor Maleficarum, and Mayaserena Ce'Nedra, will continue on
      in the tradition of UNC.</font></b></p>
      <p align="center"><b><font color="#8000FF" size="3">And so continues the story of one Guilds adventures thru<br>
                                Norrath... </font></b></p>
      &nbsp;</td>
